12.150 emacsvox-pronounce
=========================

This module implements user customizable pronunciation dictionaries for
emacsvox.  Custom pronunciations can be defined per file, per directory
and/or per major mode.  Emacsvox maintains a persistent user dictionary
upon request and loads these in new emacsvox sessions.  This module
implements the user interface to the custom dictionary as well as
providing the internal API used by the rest of emacsvox in using the
dictionary.

12.150.1 Algorithm:
-------------------

The persistent dictionary is a hash table where the hash keys are
filenames, directory names, or major-mode names.  The hash values are
association lists defining the dictionary.  Users of this module can
retrieve a dictionary made up of all applicable association lists for a
given file.

12.150.2 Emacsvox-Pronounce Commands
------------------------------------

12.150.2.1 emacsvox-pronounce-clear
...................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-pronounce-clear

     Clear all current pronunciation dictionaries.

12.150.2.2 emacsvox-pronounce-define-pronunciation
..................................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-pronounce-define-pronunciation

     Interactively define entries in the pronunciation dictionaries.
     Default term to define is delimited by region.
     First loads any persistent dictionaries if not already loaded.

12.150.2.3 emacsvox-pronounce-define-template-pronunciation
...........................................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-pronounce-define-template-pronunciation

     Interactively define template entries in the pronunciation dictionaries.
     Default term to define is delimited by region.
     First loads any persistent dictionaries if not already loaded.

12.150.2.4 emacsvox-pronounce-dispatch
......................................

 -- Command: emacsvox-pronounce-dispatch
     ‘C-e M-d’

     Pronounce Frontend

12.150.2.5 emacsvox-pronounce-edit-pronunciations
