12.215 extra-muggles
====================

MUGGLES == Emacsvox spells for power-users.  These are extra hydras that
I dont use very often, And are being moved here from emacsvox-muggles to
save time at startup.

   This module implements no new functionality -- contrast with
emacsvox-wizards.  Instead, it uses package hydra to provide convenience
key-bindings that access existing Emacsvox functionality.  You need to
install package Hydra first: ‘M-x package-install hydra’.

   Note that on newer versions of Emacs, loading this module will
attempt to automatically install package hydra if it is not found.

12.215.1 Using Hydras
---------------------

See the high-level documentation for the Hydra package by executing ‘C-h
C-j ’ hydra ‘RET’.  The documentation in this section uses the same
terminology as shown in the hydra package documentation.

12.215.2 Extra Muggles
----------------------

   • org-mode structure nav: ‘C-c C-SPC’ Navigation for org-mode.
   • View-Mode: ‘C-. v’ Temporarily behave like view-mode.
   • SmartParens: ‘C-c ,’ Smart Parens
   • m-player: ‘s-m’ Emacsvox-M-Player Commands
   • m-player: ‘s-;’ Emacsvox-M-Player muggle
   • pianobar: ‘s-'’ Emacsvox-M-pianobar Commands
   • origami: C-, / Origami bindings.
   • outliner: <C-c .> Bindings from outline-minor-mode.
   • Info-Summary: <?> in Info Info Summary Muggle
   • Vuiet Explorer: ‘C-; v’ Vuiet Music Explorer and Player

   Emacsvox automatically speaks Hydra hints when displayed.  To silence
all Hydra hints, set hydra-is-helpful to nil.  To temporarily silence
speaking of Hydra hints, Muggles can bind command
‘emacsvox-hydra-toggle-talkative’.  As an example, Muggle ‘ViewMode’
binds ‘s’ to this command.

12.215.3 Extra-Muggles Commands
-------------------------------

12.215.3.1 emacsvox-muggles-emacsvox-m-player-mode-map-cmd
..........................................................

