12.224 pip
==========

Piper TTS is an Open Source neural-net TTS engine.  This module exposes
Piper TTS to Emacs.

12.225 Piper TTS
================

  1. Sandbox for <https://github.com/rhasspy/piper>
  2. pipx install piper-tts.
  3. Set location of voice data in ‘pip-data-dir’.  Default is
     ‘~/.local/share/voices-piper’
  4. ;; Create the data directory above if needed.
  5. Run piper there using the -update-voices flag once for each desired
     voice to get the voice models.
  6. ‘M-x pip-speak’ to speak.
  7. At present ‘piper’ is not suitable for use as a primary TTS engine
     for Emacsvox, given its high latency.
  8. However it might be interesting to use it for lower-priority speech
     where quality trumps latency.

12.225.1 Pip Commands
---------------------

12.225.1.1 pip-speak
....................

 -- Command: pip-speak [Arg list not available until function definition
          is loaded.]

     Speak text

     (fn TEXT)


